# Caddy in front of kb-server: automatic HTTPS (Let's Encrypt) for $KB_DOMAIN and a
# plain reverse proxy (WebSocket upgrades on /v2/ws pass through). kb-server itself
# speaks plain HTTP on the compose network only.
#
# reverse_proxy sets X-Forwarded-For to the client's address by default (and, with no
# `trusted_proxies` of its own, drops whatever a client sent in that header). kb-server
# reads it only from addresses listed in KB_SERVER_TRUSTED_PROXIES (Caddy's address in
# docker-compose.yml), for its per-client rate limits.
#
# Caddy writes no access log unless a `log` directive is added here. If you add one,
# filter the query string: a WebSocket client may send its session token as `?token=`
# (Caddy already redacts the Authorization header).
{$KB_DOMAIN} {
	reverse_proxy kb-server:8787
}
